    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "image",
        "operation": "analyze",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite"
        },
        "text": "=You are screening an image shared in a job/gig-work Telegram group to classify what kind of payment-related image it is, if any.\n\nMessage caption/text from the poster, if any (use ONLY to help identify a paying company or payment method not visible in the image itself — never invent one): \"{{ $('Telegram Trigger').item.json.message.caption ?? '' }}\"\n\n=== ONLY DIRECT PROOF COUNTS ===\nDirect proof is any of:\n(a) a screenshot of an actual payment/banking app or wallet showing the transaction itself,\n(b) an email or in-app receipt showing transaction details,\n(c) a payout/earnings notification sent DIRECTLY BY the platform or employer to the recipient — e.g. \"Your payout of $X is on its way\", a payslip-style email, an app notification stating an amount and status. This still counts as direct proof even if the same email/message ALSO contains unrelated marketing, referral-program, or cross-sell content (e.g. \"Earn more through referrals\", an \"Explore\" button) elsewhere in the message — ignore that marketing portion and extract only from the actual payout notice,\n(d) a bot-generated notification card from THIS group's own bot (headers like \"INVOICE / BILL\" or \"VERIFIED PAYMENT\").\n\nIf the image is instead a screenshot of a social media post, chat message, or forum thread that merely TALKS ABOUT or DISPLAYS a payment as part of a longer post — recognizable by social-platform UI chrome such as: an avatar + username + \"Follow\"/role-badge header, like/comment/share/bookmark counts, a post-age label (\"8h\", \"22h\", \"2d\"), a \"Translate\" option, \"View activity\", or nested reply/comment threads — this is a REPOST/TESTIMONIAL, not direct proof, even if it contains a visible amount, a \"successful\"/\"completed\" status, or persuasive claims about earnings. Set Category to \"not_payment\" in this case, regardless of what payment-looking content is embedded inside it.\n\n=== PRODUCT / COURSE LISTINGS ARE NOT PAYMENTS ===\nAn ad or storefront-style listing for a course, ebook, service, or product (price/currency badge next to a product title or thumbnail, \"buy now\"-style layout, with NO transaction status and NO invoice framing directed at a specific buyer) is NOT a payment screenshot — set Category to \"not_payment\" even though a price/currency amount is visible.\n\nSet Category to exactly one of:\n- \"paid\": a completed payout/transfer, shown as DIRECT proof (see above) — status wording like \"Completed\", \"Successful\", \"Sent\", \"Submitted\", \"Penarikan sukses\" all count.\n- \"pending\": a payout/payment shown as DIRECT proof that is scheduled, processing, in transit, or awaiting approval — not yet completed/arrived. Includes payout notification emails saying funds are \"on its way\" or \"should appear within X business days\".\n- \"bill_invoice\": an invoice, bill, or payment request shown as DIRECT proof — money owed, not money received. Includes course/product purchase cards explicitly framed as an invoice/bill.\n- \"not_payment\": the image isn't direct payment/financial proof — including product/course/service ads, storefront listings, and social-media/chat reposts or testimonials that merely display or discuss a payment.\n- \"other\": something payment-related that doesn't fit the above.\n\nRegardless of Category, extract whatever of the following is visible — don't leave fields empty just because Category isn't \"paid\":\n- Paying_Company: the employer, client, or company the money is coming FROM (or billed BY, for invoices), if named. Empty string if not shown.\n- Amount: the amount AND currency combined into one string, currency placed where it naturally belongs (e.g. \"USDC 99.34\", \"$1,XXX.XX\", \"USD X53.47\"). If digits are blurred/covered/blacked-out/scribbled, replace each hidden digit with X following normal digit grouping — a hidden group after a thousands comma is exactly 3 X's (e.g. \"$1,XXX\", never \"$1,X\"), a hidden cents group after a decimal point is exactly 2 X's (e.g. \"$1,XXX.XX\"). If the whole amount is hidden, write \"redacted\". Empty string only if no amount appears anywhere.\n- Date: a date/time that is part of the PAYMENT CONTENT itself — e.g. \"sent on...\", an issue date, a due date, a transaction timestamp inside the message or receipt body. Do NOT use timestamps from surrounding UI chrome that aren't part of the payment content — an email/inbox app's \"received at\" time, the phone's status bar clock, a notification badge time, a social post's \"Xh\" age label, etc. If the payment content itself doesn't state a date, leave this empty — don't substitute a nearby UI timestamp. The date format should look like 1 January 2026.\n- Payment_Method: whatever best identifies how/where the money moved or is billed through — a processor/app/bank name (Airtm, PayPal, Deel, Wise, a bank name) OR a generic method (Bank Transfer, Wire, Crypto) if no named service is shown. Use whichever is actually visible; don't guess a name that isn't there. If nothing is visible in the image, check the caption text above before leaving this empty.\n\nRespond with ONLY a single valid JSON object, no markdown, no code fences, no commentary, matching exactly:\n{\n  \"Category\": string,\n  \"Paying_Company\": string,\n  \"Amount\": string,\n  \"Date\": string,\n  \"Payment_Method\": string\n}",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
